      "text": "The progress from one number to the next will be a new digit starting from the 11. \nSince 11 is a prime number with two unique factors, 29 produces the same digit, 9, in its next value. Therefore, \n$29*2=58$ with the same digit in the second position as 9 or digit 8. Add 10 to 8 to carry over the 10 to \nthe next number. Therefore, the value in the third place, will resolve itself to 8+1+11, or 8+12, which \nequals 20. Subtract 10 to carry forward to the next number. Therefore, the value of the next number will be \n20+10 or 30. Add the new digit to the 4th place, which resolves into 2+1, which equals 3. Then add 1 more \nto reach 301. 301 is the 9th number introduced by changing the 12 to the new number to obtain 58 and then adding \none. Therefore, the 10th number in the list will be 29*3, which is the 11th number in the list with digit 8 in the second \nplace, which equals 88. Then, continue adding a 9 to 88. Thus, the 11th number is $\\boxed{899}$. The answer is 899",
